    "problem_statement": "After a pthread is detached and then canceled (terminated), a subsequent pthread_join() of that thread must fail with EINVAL (the thread is not joinable), consistent with POSIX/Solaris/Linux. The test asserts the join returns a non-zero error with status == EINVAL; on the old kernel the join returns ESRCH instead because the join information is destroyed at termination time, so the assertion fails. Required behavior: joining a detached/canceled thread returns EINVAL.",
